[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Dinkeloo#cite_ref-11]  Goldberger, Paul (March 2, 2019). "Kevin Roche, Architect Who Melded Bold With Elegant, Dies at 96".  [LINK: (The New York Times) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times] . Retrieved March 2, 2019.

^  [LINK: (a) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Dinkeloo#cite_ref-Skyline_AIA_Dinkeloo_obit_1981_12-0]   [LINK: (b) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Dinkeloo#cite_ref-Skyline_AIA_Dinkeloo_obit_1981_12-1]   [LINK: (c) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Dinkeloo#cite_ref-Skyline_AIA_Dinkeloo_obit_1981_12-2]  Stephen, Suzanne, ed. (October 1981). "In Memorium: John Dinkeloo 1918-1981" (PDF). Skyline: The Architecture and Design Review. New York: Rizolli International - American Institute of Architecture: 10.  [LINK: (ISSN) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)]  0162-6981. Retrieved June 8, 2024. Even when refining, instead of pioneering, new applications of materials for architectural use, Dinkeloo was finding ways in which form and technics would continue to be inseparable-where architecture, in the best modernist tradition, would draw equally from both a formal image and a technical idea.

^  [LINK: (a) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Dinkeloo#cite_ref-Dinkeloo_and_glass_technology_13-0]   [LINK: (b) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Dinkeloo#cite_ref-Dinkeloo_and_glass_technology_13-1]   [LINK: (c) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Dinkeloo#cite_ref-Dinkeloo_and_glass_technology_13-2]  Lefer, Henry (June 1976). "Through a glass" (PDF). Progressive Architecture. 57 (6). Reinhold Publishing Company, Inc.: 49. Retrieved June 25, 2024. In fact, with the urging of such architects as Kevin Roche and John Dinkeloo—architects who have consistently pursued the greenhouse ideal—manufacturers have developed new types of glass. One need only look at the glass with strips of mirror coating, giving the effect of Venetian blinds that Roche, Dinkeloo produced for the Irwin Union Bank in Columbus, IN, to be impressed by the results of this experimentation.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Dinkeloo#cite_ref-stands_14-0]  "K of C Headquarters Stands Tall for Half a Century". Columbia. August 2019. p. 7.


